  "summary": "Dated August 3, 1964, this two-page private letter from M. R. Masani to Prof. N. G. Ranga addresses organisational difficulties facing the Swatantra Party in Bengal. Masani says he has been authorised by the Organisation Sub-Committee to replace the ineffective interim committee, headed by Patodia, with district-level grassroots activity. He reports having contacted potential Bengali leaders in Calcutta but identifies the absence of indigenous Bengali leadership as the party's principal weakness.",
