    "key_points": [
      "Masani is distressed by the failure of the Bengal organisation to establish an effective party presence over four years.",
      "The Organisation Sub-Committee has authorised him to develop grassroots activity at the district level.",
      "He considers the interim committee with Patodia as Convenor to have failed completely.",
      "Masani argues that the party cannot be built in Bengal while activity centres on Patodia and Nandi.",
      "He asks Ranga to prevent Patodia and Nandi from pursuing plans that might conflict with Masani's organisational mandate.",
      "The letter warns that continued activity along those lines could produce repercussions injurious to the party."
